```plaintext
0result.sql
```

0result.sql is preferred because  
• Numerator: sums the under‑25 population directly from the 5‑year age‑group table (`total_flag = 'A'`, `starting_age < 25`) which already contains both sexes combined, so no risk of double‑counting genders.  
• Denominator: uses the dedicated total‑population table (`midyear_population`), guaranteeing the figure is the official 2017 total for each country.  
• The join and aggregation are simple and logically consistent; the percentage is therefore accurate.  
In contrast, 1result.sql relies on the “*” row inside the same 5‑year table (equivalent but redundant), and 2result.sql sums the single‑age/sex table which may double‑count if a ‘Both sexes’ record exists.